        "evidence": "explicit",
        "evidenceText": "Answer label B is shown in the presenter notes panel."
      },
      "maxSelections": 1,
      "explanation": "If \"1011\" is sent to pin2 (interpreted bit by bit):\n\n1. For the first bit (1 → HIGH): pin1 = LOW.\n2. For the second bit (0 → LOW): pin1 = HIGH.\n3. For the third bit (1 → HIGH): pin1 = LOW.\n4. For the fourth bit (1 → HIGH): pin1 = LOW.\n\nOutput of pin1:\n\nThe sequence of outputs for pin1 is: LOW, HIGH, LOW, LOW.",
      "topicIds": [],
      "extractionConfidence": 0.98,
      "needsReview": false,
